   "title": "Paras Health to use ₹375 cr from IPO to pare debt, plans 800-bed expansion",
   "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5"
  }
 ],
 "synopsis": "Paras Healthcare plans an initial public offering worth ₹1,450 crore, comprising a ₹500 crore fresh issue and a ₹950 crore offer for sale. As part of the offer for sale, promoter Dharminder Nagar and investor Commelina Limited will pare their holdings, reducing the promoter group's stake from 72.8 per cent to 64 per cent. The company intends to use ₹375 crore from the fresh issue to partially repay existing debt and ₹125 crore for general corporate purposes. The hospital chain also plans to add 800 beds through greenfield projects in Gurugram and Ludhiana.",
